<title>HUNGARY: Hungary 7yr govt bond avr price drops to 103.08%. [CORRECTED 15:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>Hungary 7yr govt bond avr price drops to 103.08%. [CORRECTED 15:50 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average price of Hungary's seven-year government bonds was set by auction at 103.08 percent of the face value, down from 103.55 pct at an auction on March 13, the Government Debt Management Agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BONDS OF THE 2004/F SERIES</p>
<p>    First day of interest    18 March, 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   12 March, 2004 (Corrects year)</p>
<p>    Total on offer	    10,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     10,078.88 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	   10,078.88 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		11,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Average price		  103.08 pct</p>
<p>NOTE -  The bond bears a floating interest, calculated every half year, adding three percent to year-on-year consumer inflation. The interest is paid once a year, on March 12. The starting interest is 21.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
